  "description": "A lightweight, dependency-free .NET 10/.NET 11 library for creating and reading XLSX workbooks and exporting worksheet data to CSV. Trim-safe and AOT-compatible with zero reflection.",
  "iconFile": "Assets/NkkinXlsx-icon.png",
  "id": "NkkinXlsx",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-16T11:10:59.397Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "ebeasIRrAfY7aske6xJzFqXxWktfd4xx2pC6tN03wQSZUHjwrMx/22a0758P+v6/5QdIJHgcDMi8jR8AtY11cA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 109545,
  "published": "2026-11-16T10:56:20.04Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.1: no longer requires preview features (1.0.0 marked the assembly [RequiresPreviewFeatures], so apps failed to compile with CA2252). Fixes: text with control characters or unpaired surrogates no longer makes Save throw (written with Excel's _xHHHH_ escapes, decoded on read); text that looks like an escape stays literal in Excel; numbers with formats such as [Red]0.00, \"USD\" or [$-409] no longer read back as dates; cells over Excel's 32,767-character limit are refused on save with the cell address; sheet names with control characters are refused. Reader: streams worksheets and shared strings (about 3x faster and 4x less memory on large files), reads cells and rows without references, inline rich text, ISO date cells, and skips phonetic guide text. Same API as 1.0.0.\n1.0.0: net10.0 + net11.0 targets.\n0.2.x: trim- and AOT-compatible; SetRows for row enumeration; deterministic builds with snupkg symbols.",
